From 3179b41748c7f039694091a4ee8eb600865372ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoatium Build <stoatium@localhost>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:10:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ui(profile): size cards to content, fix the hover card,
 translate literals

width=3 was gridColumn "1 / 4". The profile cards are used in two grids --
the modal's three columns and the hover card's two -- so in the hover card
a hardcoded line 4 conjured a phantom third column, squeezing the banner
into a strip. "1 / -1" spans whatever the grid actually has. Same for the
actions row.

width=1 forced aspectRatio 1/1 with overflow hidden. A square is only right
when the content fills it: a "Groups" card holding one shared group drew a
single 20px avatar adrift in a large empty box, and anything taller than the
square was silently cut. Cards now size to their content.

Mutual friends and groups span the row with 32px avatars -- they are strips
of faces, not tiles.

"Mutuals", "Groups", "Bio", "Add Friend", "Accept friend request", "Cancel
friend request" and "Message" were bare literals that never reached the
catalog, so they stayed English in every locale. Four already had
translations under the same msgid; Bio and the two mutuals lists are new.
